/* ========================================
 * COMPONENTS: Dialogs
 * ========================================
 * Modal dialogs and popup styles
 * ======================================== */

/* FileSave/FileOpen (vendored Third_Party/textual_fspicker) input bar --
   the filename Input + file-type filter Select row shared by every
   FileOpen/FileSave dialog in the app (Evals export, STTS, library
   import/export, Voice Cloning, LLM model browsing, etc).
   `_conversations.tcss`'s bare, unscoped `Select { width: 100%; }` rule
   always beats `file_dialog.py`'s own `DEFAULT_CSS` regardless of source
   order -- Textual's cascade ranks EVERY CSS_PATH-sourced rule (this
   bundle) above any widget's own DEFAULT_CSS no matter how specific the
   DEFAULT_CSS selector is (same Defect 1 lesson as
   `#mcp-tools-filter-server-slot Select` / `.approval-row-decision`
   elsewhere in this bundle). Without this override, the filter Select
   claims the ENTIRE input-bar row, squeezing the filename Input down to a
   handful of columns -- observed ~5 at 235x52, where a keyboard-only
   export/save flow needs to both read and type into that field
   (task-1479). A 3-type compound selector already outranks the bare
   1-type `Select {}` rule on specificity, so no id is needed for it to
   win here. Scoped to the vendored dialogs themselves (`FileSave`/
   `FileOpen`), not the separate `EnhancedFileDialog` picker
   (`Widgets/enhanced_file_picker.py`), which composes its own Input/Select
   with its own ids and is out of scope for this fix. */
FileSave InputBar Select,
FileOpen InputBar Select {
    width: 24;
    margin-bottom: 0;
}
